      "committedDate": "2026-11-02T14:26:59Z",
      "messageBody": "Motivation: Sparse attention needs scalar UB reads, typed aliases and\nruntime-strided row transfers without private code-generator adaptations.\n\nDesign: Add checked public APIs backed by native memref and HIVM builders.\nPreserve source offsets, destination pitch and visible storage aliases.\nUse static-capacity views with dynamic transfer subviews to support\nzero-offset pointer entries, and cover the interfaces with tla_ut.\n\nRisks: Dynamic bounds and manually scheduled buffer lifetimes remain the\ncaller's responsibility. Target-specific DMA constraints still apply.\n\nAssisted-by: AI",
      "messageHeadline": "[Triton][TLA] feat: Add sparse DMA memory interfaces",
      "oid": "4a96387550889968145e01e2a66fab99f5cf9341"
    }
  ],
